======================================================================
  KEY THEOREM (discovered this session):
  Over GF(2), Edge(K_n) = Cut ⊕ Cycle iff n is ODD.
  For even n: dim(Cut ∩ Cycle) = n-2.
  The cycle-space projection v ↦ (I + L(K_n)) v mod 2
  gives a well-defined tournament → even graph map only at odd n.
  At odd n: V_even(n) = number of even graph iso classes
  on n vertices. V_t/V_e grows exponentially.
======================================================================

DONE.
